# Git Workflow

After making **huge or sweeping changes** (refactors, multi-file edits, new features), run:

```bash
git add -A
git status   # review what will be committed
git commit -m "Brief description of changes"
```

This keeps the working tree clean and creates logical checkpoints for revert or review.
